From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PiBridge <noreply@pibridge.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] displayport: re-read the sink's FEC capability in the SST DSC
 check

The DP library reads the sink's FEC capability (DPCD 0x090) once, at
detection. Some sinks NAK their first AUX reads while their display bridge
is still starting; the Pimax Crystal Super VR headset does this. The failed read leaves FEC cached as "unsupported" for the whole
session, so compoundQueryAttachSSTIsDscPossible() says DSC is impossible
and every mode above the uncompressed link bandwidth is rejected (on the
Crystal Super: all of its 7104x3840 modes, HBR3 x4, DSC 8.0 bpp needed).

Read the FEC capability again in the check when the cached value says no
and the GPU supports FEC. The check also dereferenced the native device
without a NULL test; a mode can be validated before the DP library has
found the sink (seen with an EDID override at boot), so test it first.

GPUs: RTX 50 (Blackwell). Headset: Pimax Crystal Super.
Driver: 595.99.02. Applies unchanged (git apply, not built there) to
610.57.04, 615.71.09 and 615.78.08.
Tested: RTX 5090 + Crystal Super, 7104x3840 over DP with DSC (with an
EDID override that sets 8 bpc: the headset's EDID says "undefined" colour
depth, NVKMS then uses 6 bpc and DSC refuses 6 bpc; that part is not a
driver change).

License: MIT OR GPL-2.0, as open-gpu-kernel-modules.
---
 src/common/displayport/src/dp_connectorimpl.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/common/displayport/src/dp_connectorimpl.cpp b/src/common/displayport/src/dp_connectorimpl.cpp
index caf1c8e..f140673 100644
--- a/src/common/displayport/src/dp_connectorimpl.cpp
+++ b/src/common/displayport/src/dp_connectorimpl.cpp
@@ -1976,10 +1976,23 @@ bool ConnectorImpl::compoundQueryAttachSSTIsDscPossible
     main->getDscCaps(&bGpuDscSupported);
     DeviceImpl * nativeDev = this->findDeviceInList(Address());
 
+    //
+    // The sink's FEC capability is read once, at detection. Some sinks (a VR
+    // headset whose display bridge is still starting) NAK their first AUX reads,
+    // which leaves FEC "unsupported" and DSC impossible for the whole session, so
+    // every mode above the uncompressed link bandwidth is rejected. Read it again
+    // here when the cached value says no and the GPU supports FEC.
+    //
+    if (nativeDev && !nativeDev->isFECSupported() && this->isFECSupported())
+    {
+        nativeDev->getFECSupport();
+    }
+
     if (bGpuDscSupported &&                                 // if GPU supports DSC
         this->isFECSupported() &&                           // If GPU supports FEC
         pDscParams &&                                       // if client sent DSC info
         pDscParams->bCheckWithDsc &&                        // if client wants to check with DSC
+        nativeDev &&                                        // a mode can be validated before the sink is found
         nativeDev->isDSCPossible() &&                       // if device supports DSC decompression
         (nativeDev->isFECSupported() || main->isEDP()) &&   // if device supports FEC decoding or is an DSC capable eDP panel which doesn't support FEC
         (modesetParams.modesetInfo.bitsPerComponent != 6))  // DSC doesn't support bpc = 6
